              <pre class="code"><code>{slotLine(pd.slots)}</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>(a) 40 mod 5 = 0: slot 0 (17, not it), slot 1 (40): <b>found</b> after 2 tries. (b) 22 mod 5 = 2: slots 2, 3, 4, 0, 1 all hold other keys and none is empty, so the loop tries all 5 slots and returns <b>-1</b>. A full table makes every "not found" search check every slot.</li>
            <li>(a) α = 5 / 5 = <b>1.0</b>: completely full. (b) With mod 11:
              <pre class="code"><code>{slotLine(p11.slots).split('\n').filter((l) => !l.endsWith('-')).join('\n')}</code></pre>
              Every other slot is empty, and no key collides.</li>
            <li>It <b>crashes</b> while inserting 17: <code>ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException: Index 5 out of bounds for length 5</code>. 17 mod 5 = 2; slots 2, 3, and 4 are taken, so the next try is slot 2 + 3 = 5, which does not exist. Line 8 forgot to wrap around. Fix: <code>int slot = (home + i) % m;</code>.</li>
            <li>(a) <b>Hash table</b>: many lookups by exact key. (b) <b>Not</b> a hash table: it has no order. Use a sorted structure (a BST or <code>TreeMap</code>), or sort the grades. (c) <b>Rehash</b> into a bigger table (about twice the size, a prime), so the load factor drops below 0.5.</li>
          </ol>
        </div></details>
      </div>
      <div class="paper flow" id="task">
