      <p>Not graded. Tap an answer to see if you got it, and read why.</p>
      <Quiz id="quiz-hash" questions={quiz} />
      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">Key takeaways</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Hashing turns a key into a slot number with a fixed rule, so a search can jump straight to one slot.</li>
          <li>In this course, h(k) = k mod m. A prime m spreads keys better.</li>
          <li>Collisions cannot be avoided. Separate chaining keeps a chain per bucket; open addressing tries other slots.</li>
          <li>Try i: linear (h + i) mod m; quadratic (h + i²) mod m; double hashing (h + i × step(k)) mod m.</li>
          <li>Searches follow the insert's path and stop at the key or at an empty slot, so deletes leave a "deleted" mark.</li>
          <li>Load factor α = n / m. Keep it low, and rehash into a bigger table when it gets high. Then finding a key takes about 1 or 2 tries, but a hash table keeps no order.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
